[[!comment format=mdwn
 username="joey"
 subject="""comment 6"""
 date="2026-11-12T18:59:57Z"
 content="""
The p2phttpchill branch has this implemented, except for proxied remotes which
get --proxyconnections connections per repository.

It may be that the GC hack is not actually needed to solve that. (Whew!)

The ProxyConnectionPool already supports evicting old connections as
needed, which will shut down proxied remotes cleanly. Just need to
make a single ProxyConnectionPool be shared amoung each repository state,
rather than each having its own pool.

And change the meaning of --proxyconnections to be not maximum
per repository, but overall. Then it can become a simple quantiry semaphore.
"""]]
